    "title": "Austin Residents Face Higher Utility Bills Under New City Budget - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natalie Petrovich ,\n1 days ago Many Austin residents opening their November bills are finding an unwelcome surprise: higher charges for electricity, water, and trash service tied to the city’s new FY 2025-26 budget. The rate changes, which took effect Nov. 1, apply to most customers. City estimates suggest a “typical” household will pay about $80 more a year, even as some electric account types see savings from lower wholesale pass-throughs. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
